index c16b1e2..6725291 100644
--- a/webhooks/aws/unified-webhook/README.md
+++ b/webhooks/aws/unified-webhook/README.md
@@ -36,3 +36,41 @@ Downstream: pulsar refuses to run an agent for a sender with no
 anyone, unlike a Slack/Teams channel whose membership is the access boundary.
 Carrier keywords (STOP/HELP/…) are dropped before dispatch; enable **Advanced
 Opt-Out** on the Messaging Service so Twilio sends the mandated replies.
+
+## Confluence (comments on pages)
+
+Confluence Cloud's own webhooks need an installed Connect/Forge app; a **Confluence
+Automation rule** needs none. Its **Send web request** action posts to
+`POST https://<webhook-host>/webhooks/v2/confluence?tenant_id=<uuid>&tenant=<name>` with the
+header `X-Confluence-Webhook-Secret: <CONFLUENCE_WEBHOOK_SECRET>` and a JSON body built from
+smart values:
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "comment_created",
+  "page_id": "{{page.id}}",
+  "comment_id": "{{comment.id}}",
+  "page_title": "{{page.title}}",
+  "space_key": "{{space.key}}",
+  "author_id": "{{comment.author.accountId}}",
+  "author_name": "{{comment.author.displayName}}"
+}
+```
+
+Emits `page.commented` (`comment_updated` → `page.comment_updated`; a top-level
+`event_type` wins) with flat `confluence_page_id`, `confluence_comment_id`,
+`confluence_page_title`, `confluence_space_key`, `confluence_author` in
+`structured_payload`. A Connect webhook body (`comment.container`) is read too.
+
+| Key | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `CONFLUENCE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | The shared secret the rule sends in `X-Confluence-Webhook-Secret`. |
+
+## GitHub: tenant in the URL
+
+GitHub's repo/org webhook settings cannot add headers, so besides `X-Tenant-ID` the tenant
+may come from `?tenant_id=<uuid>&tenant=<name>` on the payload URL (the header wins when
+both are sent). `structured_payload` also carries flat `github_event`, `github_action`,
+`github_repo`, `github_delivery`, `pr_number` (an `issue_comment` has one only when its
+issue is a pull request), `pr_merged`, `pr_base`, `github_comment_id` and
+`github_comment_kind` (`issue` / `line` / `review`).
